<p>Insurance claims are supposed to bring relief after property damage. In practice, they often bring delays, confusing letters, and estimates that do not match what the repairs actually cost. McAllen Public Adjuster exists to give homeowners and business owners in McAllen, Hidalgo County, and the surrounding Rio Grande Valley (RGV) someone in their corner during that process: a licensed public adjuster who works for the policyholder, not the insurance company.</p>
<p>Your insurer has its own adjusters, estimators, and claim reviewers. We believe you deserve informed representation, too.</p>

<h2>Who operates McAllen Public Adjuster</h2>
<p>McAllen Public Adjuster is a public adjusting service of <strong>[[company]]</strong>, licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance (TDI license #[[license]]). We serve McAllen, Hidalgo County, and nearby Rio Grande Valley communities, and we meet clients at their damaged property rather than at a storefront office.</p>
<p>Claims are led by <a href="/author/joseph-dittman/">Joseph Dittman</a>, a licensed Texas public adjuster, certified insurance appraiser, insurance umpire, and expert witness. His background includes carrier-side adjusting, public adjusting, appraisal work, expert witness support, and hands-on construction experience, across residential, commercial, storm, hail, wind, water, fire, hurricane, and catastrophe losses. He also reviews the articles published on this site.</p>

